slang: binsof of a hierarchical cross item

`cross cp_y, cfg.vif.x { ignore_bins i = binsof(cfg.vif.x) ...; }` in a class covergroup:
the hierarchical cross item is slang's own extension (-Wnonstandard-hierarchical-cross),
but binsof(cfg.vif.x) then bound cfg as in a static context: "invalid use of non-static
class property 'cfg'". ConditionBinsSelectExpr::fromSyntax now matches a binsof target
against the text of its cross's implicit items before binding it as a name.
CoverpointSymbol::isImplicitlyDeclared() is new. Found in OpenTitan's sysrst_ctrl DV.
Applies on top of 0016.

